>I just started playing NetHack (3.1 Amiga), I keep starving to death.  How
>do I find food?  I've tried to eat the corpses of my victims, but its
>usually bad for me, what do I do?  What is the best character?  Is this
>similar to Moria?  Thanks.

Very mild spoilers:

While you're still at the starving-to-death stage of NetHack, the
best character is the barbarian, because they're poison resistent
and they fight well.  Valkyries are slightly better once you're
good enough to get poison resistance on your own, because they 
get a better artifact from Odin than barbarians do from Crom, 
and because they start with a +3 shield, which is nice when you
last long enough to find armor to go with it.

Eat corpses quickly.  Remember which ones damage or poison you
(though poisoning won't hurt a barbarian) and especially remember
which ones grant you useful intrinsics.  (There is a random chance
for most corpses, so don't despair if it isn't consistent.)  Never
eat an old corpse, unless you have a blessed unicorn horn handy.
If you're starving, pray.  (Always try to pray if death impends.)

Keep moving fast.  Sitting around too long is a good way to starve.
There are a lot of tasty gnomes in the dwarvish mines, and once you
know how to survive there you're in good shape.

This game is like Moria, with some differences.  It has a reasonably
quick finish once you know what you're doing; you won't play the
same character for months.  There is much more clever coding, with
lots of depth (check the YAFM posts here every day).  I like NetHack
better, because I can pick it up, ascend in a weekend, and put it
away for a month.  Moria drags too much for that.

